const e={"seo.purpose":"Who the address translator is for","seo.purpose.p1":"People who need a Taiwan address in English and do not want to paste it into another website.","seo.purpose.p2":"Useful for forms and mail when the road should come from a postal glossary and unknown building names should stay unchanged.","seo.why":"Why this translator","seo.why.p1":"Road names come from Chunghwa Post’s bilingual list on the government open-data portal, under the Open Government Data License, version 1.","seo.why.li1":"District names come from Chunghwa Post’s public county file. The full 3+3 doorplate database requires an application and is not included.","seo.why.li2":"District names come from open-data set 5949. Villages and named lanes had no redistribution license we could verify, so they are left untranslated.","seo.why.li3":"A missing road, building, or village is not filled with guessed pinyin, and a partial result is not shown as a finished translation. 3+3 postal codes are out of scope.","seo.why.p2":"The address is matched in your browser and is not sent to Chunghwa Post or any other server.","seo.faq":"Address questions","seo.faq.q1":"Does every road have an English name?","seo.faq.q1a":"The road file has about 30,000 entries. A missing road is not replaced with guessed pinyin.","seo.faq.q2":"What about floors, lanes, and alleys?","seo.faq.q2a":"Numbers, floors, lanes, and alleys are split into No., F, Ln., and Aly. This is not an official doorplate certificate.","seo.faq.q3":"What about a building name?","seo.faq.q3a":"A building, campus, or company that is not in the glossary is listed as untranslated.","seo.faq.q4":"Is this the official English form?","seo.faq.q4a":"No. It is a reference from the published files. The agency’s current notice is what counts for an official rendering."};export{e as default};
//# sourceMappingURL=address-en-CiHmVUGL.js.map
